# The runtimeVersion "fingerprint" policy hashes config plugins, native config
# (google-services.json, GoogleService-Info.plist) and other sources by CONTENT.
# CI builds on Linux (LF); a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true would hash
# CRLF files, compute a different runtime, and an `eas update` from it would
# never reach the installed binaries. Force LF everywhere in the app.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.p8 binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
